- `vue-no-async-component`: This rule disallows using asynchronous components in Vue.js. Asynchronous components add a bit of complexity to your application and can negatively impact performance, so it's recommended to only use them when necessary. By default, async components in Vue.js are loaded dynamically using the `async` component option, which returns a Promise that resolves to a component definition once it's loaded. You can read more about it in the Vue.js documentation: [https://vuejs.org/v2/guide/component-dynamics.html#Async-Components]

- `vue/valid-template-ref`: This rule ensures that template references are valid, meaning they only reference existing components or data properties. This helps catch potential typos or errors that may occur if you reference nonexistent data or components.

